|Eduardo Artés, presidential candidate for the Communist Party (Proletarian Action), confirmed in December 2024 that he would make a third bid for the presidency, stating that his campaign seeks to reform Chile and end what he calls the country's "political duopoly".<ref name="CNN-20241217" /> Because his party is not legally registered nationwide, he was required to gather over 35,000 signatures to qualify as an independent. Shortly before the registration deadline in August 2025, his campaign announced it had met this requirement,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Al filo del plazo, Eduardo Artés logró las firmas para ser nuevamente candidato presidencial |url=https://cooperativa.cl/noticias/pais/politica/presidenciales/al-filo-del-plazo-eduardo-artes-logro-las-firmas-para-ser-nuevamente/2025-08-17/221649.html |access-date=19 August 2025 |website=Cooperativa.cl |language=Spanish}}</ref> and he officially registered with Servel on 19 August 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Martínez |first=Roberto |date=19 August 2025 |title=Con duras críticas a Jara: Eduardo Artés inscribe su candidatura presidencial |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/con-duras-criticas-a-jara-eduardo-artes-inscribe-su-candidatura-presidencial/ |access-date=19 August 2025 |website=La Tercera |language=es}}</ref>
