|[[Populism]]<br>[[E-democracy]]
|<ref name="Gonzalez-2025">{{Cite web |last=Gonzalez |first=Camila Muñoz |date=6 May 2025 |title=PDG oficializa candidatura presidencial de Franco Parisi: irá directamente a primera vuelta |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/05/06/pdg-oficializa-candidatura-presidencial-de-franco-parisi-ira-directamente-a-primera-vuelta.shtml |access-date=7 May 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref>
|Franco Parisi, presidential candidate for the Party of the People (PDG), was officially proclaimed by his party on 6 May 2025 at the [[Former National Congress of Chile building|Santiago Congress]] headquarters, marking the start of his third presidential bid. He criticized both left- and right-wing parties for prioritizing their own interests over the middle class and expressed his goal of reaching a second-round runoff while winning parliamentary seats for his party.<ref name="Gonzalez-2025" /> Parisi officially registered his candidacy with Servel on 18 August 2025, asserting that "the polls are lying" and highlighting the influence of his parliamentary candidates, including deputy [[Pamela Jiles (politician)|Pamela Jiles]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 August 2025 |title=Parisi inscribe candidatura: Acusa que "encuestas mienten" y realza figura de Pamela Jiles |url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2025/08/18/1175282/franco-parisi-inscribe-candidatura-presidencial.html |access-date=18 August 2025 |website=Emol |language=Spanish}}</ref>
|}

=== Withdrawn ===
* [[Félix González Gatica|Félix González]] ([[Green Ecologist Party (Chile)|Green Ecologist Party]]), deputy for District 20 in the [[Biobío Region]], announced his presidential bid on 6 January 2025, saying, "we have decided to collect the signatures to register an ecologist candidacy, because environmental issues are absent from the public agenda." He emphasized urgent social and climate security, adding, "we have the obligation to raise pensions... and face fires, floods, and droughts."<ref>{{Cite web |author=Martín Contreras |date=6 January 2025 |title=Diputado Félix González anuncia su candidatura presidencial por el Partido Ecologista Verde |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/diputado-felix-gonzalez-anuncia-su-candidatura-presidencial-por-el-partido-ecologista-verde/AVNHFDKYDRH33NHB5IVRBU35Z4/ |access-date=30 April 2025 |website=La Tercera |language=es}}</ref> González ultimately did not register and did not appear on the November 2025 ballot.<ref name="Martínez-2025b">{{Cite web |last=Martínez |first=Roberto |date=19 August 2025 |title=Los ocho aspirantes a La Moneda que inscribieron sus candidaturas en el Servel |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/los-ocho-aspirantes-a-la-moneda-que-inscribieron-sus-candidaturas-en-el-servel/ |access-date=19 August 2025 |website=La Tercera |language=es}}</ref>
* [[Vlado Mirosevic]] ([[Liberal Party of Chile (2013)|Liberal Party]], PL), deputy for District 1 in the [[Arica y Parinacota Region|Arica and Parinacota Region]], was proclaimed his party's presidential candidate on 12 October 2024 and planned to run in the center-left primaries. But with the Liberal Party lacking national status, it needed 35,361 signatures to validate his candidacy; by 31 March, it had only 9,851 members. Mirosevic withdrew on 16 April 2025 and endorsed Carolina Tohá.<ref name="González-2025a">{{Cite web |last=González |first=Antonio |date=16 April 2025 |title=Vlado Mirosevic abandona carrera presidencial y respaldará a Carolina Tohá |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/16/vlado-mirosevic-abandona-carrera-presidencial-y-respaldara-a-carolina-toha.shtml |access-date=17 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref> He denied the signature shortfall was the reason, arguing that multiple candidates from the PS, PPD, and PL risked handing victory to the Communist Party, and called Tohá the most competitive option.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Diputado Mirosevic: "Carolina Tohá hoy es la candidata más competitiva para ganarle a las derechas" |url=https://tele13radio.cl/show/entrevista-de-conexion-tele13/episode/diputado-mirosevic-carolina-toha-hoy-es-la-candidata-mas-competitiva-para-ganarle-a-las-derechas- |date=18 April 2025 |access-date=20 April 2025 |website=Tele13 Radio}}</ref>
* [[Francesca Muñoz]] ([[Christian Social Party (Chile)|Christian Social Party]], PSC), deputy for District 20 in the Biobío Region, was proclaimed her party's presidential candidate on 29 April 2025, following the resignation of Senator [[Rojo Edwards]] and amid a new alliance with the Republican and National Libertarian parties.<ref>{{Cite web |date=29 April 2025 |title=Surge candidatura presidencial evangélica en la derecha: PSC proclama a diputada Francesca Muñoz |url=https://www.elmostrador.cl/noticias/pais/2025/04/29/surge-candidatura-presidencial-evangelica-en-la-derecha-psc-proclama-a-diputada-francesca-munoz/ |access-date=30 April 2025 |website=El Mostrador |language=es}}</ref> But on 30 June, she ended her bid and endorsed [[José Antonio Kast]], calling the moment one that "demands brave, generous, and responsible decisions," and urging her supporters to back his candidacy.<ref>{{Cite news |date=30 June 2025 |title=Francesca Muñoz (PSC) baja su candidatura presidencial para entregar apoyo a José Antonio Kast |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/06/30/por-amor-a-chile-francesca-munoz-anuncia-respaldo-del-partido-social-cristiano-a-jose-antonio-kast.shtml |access-date=30 June 2025 |work=[[Radio Bío-Bío]]}}</ref>
* [[Ximena Rincón]] ([[Democrats (Chile)|Demócratas)]], senator for the [[Maule Region]], was proclaimed as the party's presidential candidate on 15 March 2025.<ref name="Emol-2025c">{{Cite web |date=15 March 2025 |title=Demócratas proclama a Ximena Rincón como su candidata presidencial y explorará posibilidad de primarias |url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2025/03/15/1160516/democratas-ximena-rincon-candidata.html |access-date=16 March 2025 |website=Emol |language=Spanish}}</ref> The party indicated it would explore the possibility of joining a primary with other political forces, emphasizing a centrist path "far from the extremes" and aiming for broader parliamentary representation. Rincón framed her prospective campaign around dialogue and moderation, asserting that Chile could "once again be admired and respected around the world."<ref name="Emol-2025c" /> However, she ultimately did not register her candidacy with Servel and therefore did not appear on the ballot for the November 2025 election.<ref name="Martínez-2025b" />
* Marcelo Trivelli (independent, ex-DC), former intendant of the [[Santiago Metropolitan Region]], ended his presidential bid on 31 July 2025 after failing to gather the 36,000 signatures required to run as an independent. He acknowledged the lack of both citizen support and backing from the Christian Democratic Party, which instead endorsed Jeannette Jara. Trivelli criticized the DC for "abandoning its historic convictions" and stated he would continue working on initiatives promoting social cohesion.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Quiroz |first=Nelson |date=31 July 2025 |title=Se baja candidato presidencial: no alcanzó a reunir las firmas necesarias para postular |url=https://www.adnradio.cl/2025/07/31/se-baja-candidato-presidencial-no-alcanzo-a-reunir-las-firmas-necesarias-para-postular/ |access-date=1 August 2025 |website=ADN Radio |language=es}}</ref>
* [[Alberto Undurraga]] ([[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|Christian Democratic Party]], DC), deputy for District 8 and party president, formally withdrew his presidential candidacy on 10 May 2025 during a National Council meeting, following mounting internal criticism and isolation from broader center-left alliances.<ref name="Fuentes-2025">{{Cite web |last=Fuentes |first=Cristóbal |date=10 May 2025 |title=Alberto Undurraga depone candidatura presidencial en medio de junta nacional de la DC |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/alberto-undurraga-depone-candidatura-presidencial-en-medio-de-junta-nacional-de-la-dc/ |access-date=11 May 2025 |website=La Tercera |language=es}}</ref> Though previously proclaimed by the party to run in primaries, the DC's Supreme Tribunal annulled the mandate after no pact was reached and the primary deadline passed.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 May 2025 |title=Tribunal Supremo de la DC declara cesada la candidatura presidencial de Alberto Undurraga |url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2025/05/03/1165294/candidatura-dc-alberto-undurraga-presidencial.html |access-date=4 May 2025 |website=Emol |language=Spanish}}</ref> Amid growing dissent and key figures like [[Ignacio Walker]] and [[Genaro Arriagada]] endorsing Carolina Tohá, Undurraga acknowledged that internal conditions were not conducive to a viable candidacy. He cited the need to avoid damaging the party and pledged to focus on parliamentary negotiations and promoting the DC's programmatic agenda.<ref name="Fuentes-2025" />
* [[Paulina Vodanovic]] ([[Socialist Party of Chile|Socialist Party]], PS), senator for the Maule Region and PS president, withdrew her presidential candidacy on 28 April 2025, just two weeks after being unanimously proclaimed by the party's central committee.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Silva |first=Constanza Carrillo |date=28 April 2025 |title=Paulina Vodanovic (PS) baja su candidatura presidencial previo a inscripción de primarias |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/28/paulina-vodanovic-ps-habria-bajado-su-candidatura-presidencial-previo-a-inscripcion-de-primarias.shtml |access-date=29 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref> She cited the lack of support from other parties and the need to back a unified candidacy within the center-left, which consolidated around Carolina Tohá. Vodanovic stated that continuing her campaign would have required political conditions that did not materialize and emphasized the importance of unity against the right.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fuentes |first=Samuel |date=28 April 2025 |title=Paulina Vodanovic (PS) atribuye baja de su candidatura a falta de apoyo en otros partidos |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/28/paulina-vodanovic-ps-atribuye-baja-de-su-candidatura-a-falta-de-apoyo-en-otros-partidos.shtml |access-date=29 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref>

=== Declined ===
* [[Michelle Bachelet]] ([[Socialist Party of Chile|Socialist Party]]), former [[president of Chile]] (2006–2010, 2014–2018), announced on 5 March 2025 that she would not run for a third term, stating that "good politics demands renewal." Her decision ended months of speculation within the ruling coalition. In a statement from her foundation Horizonte Ciudadano, she said others in her sector were "valuable and capable", and pledged to support whoever is ultimately chosen to represent the center-left in the November election.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bachelet se baja de la carrera presidencial: "La buena política exige renovación" |url=https://cooperativa.cl/noticias/pais/politica/presidenciales/bachelet-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial-la-buena-politica-exige/2025-03-05/121558.html |access-date=4 April 2025 |website=Cooperativa.cl |language=es}}</ref>
* [[Rodolfo Carter]] (UDI–Chile Vamos), former [[Alcalde|mayor]] of [[La Florida, Chile|La Florida]]<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 March 2025 |title=Rodolfo Carter (Ind.): "Si Chile Vamos no hace primarias, no veo espacio para estar en esa coalición como candidato a parlamentario" |url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2025/03/09/1159847/rodolfo-carter-elecciones-chile-vamos.html |access-date=7 June 2025 |website=Emol |language=Spanish}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Silva |first=Daniela |date=11 June 2025 |title=Rodolfo Carter anuncia que se suma al equipo de José Antonio Kast |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/rodolfo-carter-anuncia-que-se-suma-al-equipo-de-jose-antonio-kast/ |access-date=11 June 2025 |website=La Tercera |language=es}}</ref>
* [[Rojo Edwards]] ([[Christian Social Party (Chile)|Christian Social Party]], PSC), senator for [[Santiago Metropolitan Region|Santiago]], was briefly considered a potential presidential candidate by the PSC. In an initial internal vote, he was selected without unanimous support from the party's parliamentary members. However, at a second meeting, Edwards rejected the political guidelines set by the PSC for its presidential nominee. On 23 April 2025, the party's national leadership revoked his candidacy, citing the need for a candidate aligned with its political project.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Silva |first=Constanza Carrillo |date=24 April 2025 |title=Partido Social Cristiano (PSC) descarta llevar al senador Rojo Edwards como candidato presidencial |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/24/partido-social-cristiano-psc-descarta-llevar-al-senador-rojo-edwards-como-candidato-presidencial.shtml |access-date=25 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref> On 28 April 2025, he resigned from the party.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Friz |first=Génesis |date=28 April 2025 |title=Rojo Edwards renuncia al Partido Social Cristiano tras ser descartado como candidato presidencial |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/28/rojo-edwards-renuncia-al-partido-social-cristiano-tras-ser-descartado-como-candidato-presidencial.shtml |access-date=29 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref>
* [[Daniel Jadue]] ([[Communist Party of Chile|Communist Party]]), former mayor of [[Recoleta, Chile|Recoleta]], declined to pursue a presidential bid after his party proclaimed Labor Minister Jeannette Jara as its candidate on 5 April 2025. Jadue, under [[house arrest]] in connection with the "People's Pharmacies" case, had previously expressed interest in returning to the race. Communist Party president [[Lautaro Carmona]] announced that Jadue would instead run for deputy in the 9th district, replacing [[Karol Cariola]], who is seeking a Senate seat in Valparaíso.<ref>{{Cite web |last=González |first=Alberto |date=5 April 2025 |title=PC anuncia candidatura a diputado de Daniel Jadue tras ratificar carrera presidencial de ministra Jara |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/nacional/chile/2025/04/05/pc-anuncia-candidatura-a-diputado-de-daniel-jadue-tras-ratificar-carrera-presidencial-de-ministra-jara.shtml |access-date=6 April 2025 |website=BioBioChile |language=es}}</ref> However, that deputy candidacy did not materialize either because the [[Election Certification Tribunal]] (Tricel) excluded Jadue from the electoral register and barred him from appearing on the ballot, effectively preventing him from running for deputy.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-10-16 |title=Portazo definitivo: Tricel rechaza solicitud de Jadue y no podrá ser candidato a diputado |url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2025/10/16/1180646/tricel-jadue-no-candidato.html |access-date=2025-12-18 |website=Emol |language=Spanish}}</ref>
