* [[Claudio Orrego]] (independent, ex-[[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|DC]]), re-elected [[governor of the Santiago Metropolitan Region]] on 24 November 2024, declined to pursue a presidential candidacy despite speculation following his electoral victory. In a press conference after meeting President Gabriel Boric at [[La Moneda Palace|La Moneda]], Orrego ruled out a presidential run, stating, "My only plan is to be governor for the next four years," and said, "We'll have to look for other leaderships."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Thomson |first=Javier |date=25 November 2024 |title=Orrego descartó candidatura presidencial tras triunfo en la RM: "Mi plan es ser gobernador los cuatro años" |url=https://www.t13.cl/noticia/politica/elecciones-2024/orrego-descarto-candidatura-presidencial-tras-triunfo-rm-mi-plan-ser-gobernador-25-11 |access-date=26 January 2025 |website=T13 |language=es}}</ref>
