==Parliamentary candidates==
On 1 September 2025, all candidates for the Chamber of Deputies and the Senate were announced; 1,091 candidates for the Chamber of Deputies and 130 for the Senate:<ref name="parlcan" >{{cite news |last1=Dote |first1=Sebastián |title=Quiénes son los candidatos a diputados y senadores para las elecciones parlamentarias de Chile 2025 |url=https://elpais.com/chile/2025-11-13/quienes-son-los-candidatos-a-diputados-y-senadores-para-las-elecciones-parlamentarias-de-chile-2025.html |access-date=16 December 2025 |date=13 November 2025}}</ref>
*[[Change for Chile]]: Coalition of right-wing parties formed by the Republican Party, the Social Christian Party (PSC), and the National Libertarian Party (PNL).<ref name="parlcan" />
*[[Unidad por Chile]]: Coalition of the ruling center-left and left-wing parties: Frente Amplio (FA); the Communist Party (PC); the Socialist Party (PS); the Party for Democracy (PPD); the Radical Party (PR); the Liberal Party (PL); and the Christian Democrats (DC), the latter of which is not part of Boric's government.<ref name="parlcan" />
*[[Chile Grande y Unido]]: right-wing coalition of the traditional right-wing Chilean parties composed of National Renewal (RN); the Independent Democratic Union (UDI); Political Evolution (Evópoli), and Democrats.<ref name="parlcan" />
*[[Greens, Regionalists and Humanists]]: coalition formed by the Regionalist Green Social Federation (FRVS) and Humanist Action (AH).<ref name="parlcan" />
*[[Popular Ecologist, Animalist, and Humanist Left]]: coalition formed by the Humanist Party (PH) and the Equality Party (PI).<ref name="parlcan" />

==Campaign==
===First round===
The campaign for the general election officially began on 17 September 2025 and with eight presidential candidates, the main contest was between Jeannette Jara and José Antonio Kast.<ref>{{cite news |title=Comenzó la campaña electoral en Chile: ocho candidatos y una polarizada disputa entre Jara y Kast |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/mundo/2025/09/17/comenzo-la-campana-electoral-en-chile-ocho-candidatos-y-una-polarizada-disputa-entre-jara-y-kast/ |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=Infobae |date=17 September 2025}}</ref>

A polarising election, the campaign's main concerns were rising gang violence and migration from [[Venezuela]], rather than traditional economic or social issues.<ref>{{cite web | title='Make Chile Great Again': Insecurity marks the Chilean elections | date=15 November 2025 | url=https://www.euronews.com/2025/11/15/make-chile-great-again-security-and-migration-dominate-the-most-tense-election-in-decades }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | title=Chile votes for next president in contest dominated by crime and migration fears | work=The Guardian | date=16 November 2025 | url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/nov/16/chile-election-president-crime-migration-fears }}</ref> 

Among Kast's campaign pledges were cuts to public spending and the creation of a police force against illegal migration inspired by the [[United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Hard-right candidate Jose Antonio Kast wins Chile presidential election |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20251214-hard-right-candidate-jose-antonio-kast-wins-chile-presidential-election |website=France 24 |access-date=15 December 2025 |date=15 December 2025}}</ref> Analysts also expected the results could pave way for more market friendly initiatives as Kast was favored to win.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Chile peso firms, stocks rally after right-wing tilt in Sunday elections |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/chile-vote-sets-stage-cautious-market-rally-strong-far-right-showing-2025-11-17/ |website=Reuters}}</ref>

In general terms, right-wing and far-right parties proposed fiscal austerity measures, promotion of private investment, reduction of the state and tough security policies such as militarization, mass deportations and police defense.<ref name="pais">{{cite news |title=Compare las propuestas de los candidatos a la presidencia de Chile |url=https://elpais.com/chile/2025-11-16/compare-las-propuestas-de-los-candidatos-a-la-presidencia-de-chile.html |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=[[El País]] |date=16 November 2025}}</ref> Jara, for her part, advocated for greater state intervention, expansion of social benefits such as basic income, regulation of prices for essential services, strengthening gun control, and temporary biometric registration for immigrants.<ref name="pais" />

===Second round===
The campaign for the second round began on 17 November.<ref name="euronews2">{{cite news |title=Inicia la campaña en Chile de cara a la segunda vuelta |url=https://www.dw.com/es/inicia-la-campa%C3%B1a-en-chile-de-cara-a-balotaje-con-kast-de-favorito/a-74784964 |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=Euronews |date=18 November 2025}}</ref> Jeannette Jara started it with an event involving women in the [[La Pintana]] neighborhood of Santiago while José Antonio Kast started his campaign in the city of [[Temuco]].<ref name="euronews2" />

Insecurity was once again the key issue of the campaign, with Jara declaring that she would strengthen the police force, lift banking secrecy in order to track down money linked to drug trafficking, and reclaim neighborhoods from criminal gangs.<ref name="euronews2" /> For his part, Kast, speaking from Temuco, the capital of a region militarized since 2022 due to violence from criminal gangs, promised to deport migrants and erect a "border shield".<ref name="euronews2" />

The main televised debate between the two candidates took place on the evening of 9 December and was organized by the National Television Association (Anatel), which, according to Anatel, was watched by over seven million people.<ref>{{cite web |title=Debate Anatel alcanzó a más de 7 millones de personas, consolidándose como uno de los eventos más masivos y vistos del año |url=https://anatel.cl/debate-anatel-alcanzo-a-mas-de-7-millones-de-personas-consolidandose-como-uno-de-los-eventos-mas-masivos-y-vistos-del-ano/?utm_source=chatgpt.com |website=Anatel |access-date=16 December 2025 |date=10 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Debate Anatel: Jara y Kast se enfrentan en el último cara a cara antes de las elecciones |url=https://cooperativa.cl/noticias/pais/politica/presidenciales/debate-anatel-jara-y-kast-se-enfrentan-en-el-ultimo-cara-a-cara-antes/2025-12-09/084722.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=[[Radio Cooperativa]] |date=9 December 2025}}</ref>

Throughout his campaign, Kast used [[bulletproof glass]] at his rallies, a fact that was criticized by Jara.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gómez S. |first1=Rodrigo |title=Kast defiende uso de vidrio blindado ante críticas de Jara y descarta cambio de estrategia en debate Anatel |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/kast-defiende-uso-de-vidrio-blindado-ante-criticas-de-jara-y-descarta-cambio-de-estrategia-en-debate-anatel/ |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=La Tercera |date=10 December 2025}}</ref>

