==Results==
===President===
Jara emerged as the leading candidate in the first round with 27% of the vote, followed closely by José Antonio Kast with 24%.<ref name="euronews">{{cite news |last1=Iniguez de Onzono |first1=Javier |title=Presidenciales de Chile: Jara vence por la mínima al ultraderechista Kast en primera vuelta |url=https://es.euronews.com/2025/11/17/jara-vence-por-la-minima-a-kast-en-primera-vuelta |access-date=15 December 2025 |work=[[Euronews]] |date=17 November 2025}}</ref> However, no candidate obtained the required majority to win the presidency outright. As a result, the election proceeded to a runoff between Jeannette Jara and José Antonio Kast on 14 December 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Chile's hard-right holds the upper hand as presidential election goes to a tense runoff |url=https://apnews.com/article/chile-elections-jose-antonio-kast-jara-gabriel-boric-trump-e09ac673bfa15364251a5d324b97dc41 |last=Debre |first=Isabel |date=17 November 2025 |access-date=17 November 2025 |website=[[AP News]]}}</ref> Third place went to Franco Parisi, who obtained 20% of the vote, a surprising result given he had been polling at under 10%.<ref name="bbc1">{{cite news |last1=Caro |first1=Isabel |title=Franco Parisi, el candidato antisistema que sorprendió al ser tercero en las elecciones de Chile y cuyos votos serán clave para el balotaje entre Kast y Jara |url=https://www.bbc.com/mundo/articles/cz7px5v5720o |access-date=15 December 2025 |work=[[BBC Mundo]] |date=17 November 2025 |language=es}}</ref> Kaiser received 14% of the vote, and fifth place went to Evelyn Matthei, who received 12% of the vote, a significant defeat as she was expected to come third and had led the polls for several months at one point in the campaign.<ref name="euronews" /><ref>{{cite news |last1=Artaza |first1=Francisco |title=300 días para perder una elección: La historia íntima de la derrota de Matthei |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/300-dias-para-perder-una-eleccion-la-historia-intima-de-la-derrota-de-matthei/ |access-date=15 December 2025 |work=[[La Tercera]] |date=23 November 2025}}</ref> The other candidates received less than 5% of the votes.<ref name="bbc1" />

In his third attempt to become president of Chile, Kast won the second round with 58% of the vote, marking the most significant shift to the right since the end of the [[Military dictatorship of Chile|Pinochet dictatorship]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wells |first1=Ione |title=Chile elects far-right José Antonio Kast as next president |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0kde07lvvro |access-date=15 December 2025 |work=BBC News |date=15 December 2025}}</ref> He received the second-highest percentage of the vote since Chile's transition to democracy. Kast received 7.2 million votes, the highest ever vote total in Chile's history. He won all [[Regions of Chile|regions]] of the country, with Jara only winning the overseas vote.<ref name="tercera1">{{Cite web |title=José Antonio Kast supera a Gabriel Boric y se convierte en el Presidente electo con más votos en la historia de Chile |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/jose-antonio-kast-es-el-presidente-electo-con-mas-votos-de-la-historia-de-chile/ |website=Latercera}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Jara gana en la votación en el extranjero, pero reduce el porcentaje de apoyo a Boric en la elección contra Kast el 2021 |url=https://www.latercera.com/nacional/noticia/jara-gana-en-la-votacion-en-el-extranjero-pero-reduce-el-porcentaje-de-apoyo-obtenido-por-boric-en-la-eleccion-contra-kast-el-2021/ |access-date=15 December 2025 |work=La Tercera |date=14 December 2025}}</ref>

