=== Senate ===
In the Senate, 23 seats were renewed. The election maintained the overall ideological balance seen in 2021, with right-leaning and left-leaning parties each controlling 25 seats when counting independents. The main changes were internal to each bloc: Unidad por Chile unified the former center-left and left coalitions without altering their combined seat total, while the right experienced a shift in influence as the Republican Party expanded and the Independent Democratic Union declined.<ref name="uchile">{{cite news |title=Derecha empató con oficialismo en Senado y rozó la mayoría simple en la Cámara |url=https://radio.uchile.cl/2025/11/17/derecha-empato-con-oficialismo-en-senado-y-rozo-la-mayoria-simple-en-la-camara/ |access-date=16 December 2025 |work={{ill|Radio Universidad de Chile|es}} |date=17 November 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=La coalición de izquierda Unidad por Chile, la más votada en las elecciones legislativas chilenas |url=https://www.europapress.es/internacional/noticia-coalicion-izquierda-unidad-chile-mas-votada-elecciones-legislativas-chilenas-20251117080829.html |access-date=16 December 2025 |work=[[Europapress]] |date=17 November 2025}}</ref>

